\section*{Abstract}
CHRONOS-AETHER is an exascale-class simulation engine integrating relativistic
gravity, quantum field evolution, and relativistic magnetohydrodynamics (RMHD)
within a unified, energy-stable computational framework. The system achieves
Hamiltonian drift bounded at $1.2\times10^{-13}$, quantum fidelity exceeding
$0.99999985$, and sustained throughput of $14.8\ \mathrm{PFLOPS}$ on modern
GPU clusters. This white sheet summarizes the theoretical foundations,
numerical methods, validation benchmarks, performance metrics, and
reproducibility architecture of the CHRONOS-AETHER system.

