\section{Theoretical Foundations}

\subsection{Relativistic Gravity}
The gravitational subsystem solves the post-Newtonian-expanded relaxed Einstein
equations. The EIH equations of motion are implemented through:
\[
m_a \frac{d^2\mathbf{x}_a}{dt^2}
= \mathbf{F}_a^{\mathrm{Newton}}
+ \mathbf{F}_a^{(1\mathrm{PN})}
+ \mathbf{F}_a^{(2\mathrm{PN})}
+ \mathbf{F}_a^{(3\mathrm{PN})}
+ \mathbf{F}_a^{(3.5\mathrm{PN})}.
\]
Symplectic integration preserves a shadow Hamiltonian, yielding bounded
non-secular drift.

\subsection{Quantum Field Evolution}
Quantum fields evolve according to the covariant Dirac equation:
\[
\left(i\gamma^\mu\nabla_\mu - m\right)\psi = 0.
\]
A split-operator spectral propagator ensures norm preservation:
\[
\psi(t+\Delta t)
\approx e^{-i\hat{V}\Delta t/2}
e^{-i\hat{T}\Delta t}
e^{-i\hat{V}\Delta t/2}\psi(t).
\]

\subsection{Relativistic Magnetohydrodynamics}
RMHD equations are solved in conservation form:
\[
\frac{\partial\mathbf{U}}{\partial t}
+ \nabla\cdot\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{U})
= \mathbf{S}(\mathbf{U}),
\]
with divergence cleaning via a generalized Lagrange multiplier method. CFL
stability is enforced through:
\[
\Delta t < \frac{\Delta x}{c_s + v_A}.
\]

